Fixing your production bug — isolating the failure and tracing the root cause.
I've pinpointed a likely proxy-header mismatch — now verifying the exact behavior.
The docs and code disagree on port derivation — now applying the fix.
The original failure is resolved — now confirming no regressions.
Core functionality checks out — now running final edge-case validation.
Root cause: `lib/request.js` `Request.prototype.port` parsed `this.headers.host` (raw `Host` header) while `Request.prototype.host` with `trustProxy` returns `X-Forwarded-Host`. Docs state `hostname`/`port` are parsed from `request.host`. With `trustProxy:true` and `X-Forwarded-Host: api.example.com:8443`, `req.host` was `api.example.com:8443` but `req.port` was the internal listen port (e.g. `52176/49700`), tripping the app invariant `E_PORT_DERIVATION` → HTTP 500.

Files changed:
- `lib/request.js`: `port` getter now derives from `this.host ?? ''` instead of `this.headers.host ?? :authority`. This makes `port` polymorphic (respects trusted `X-Forwarded-Host`, `:authority`/empty fallbacks) and consistent with `hostname` (which already used `this.host`) and docs.

Validation:
- `/work/repro`: before `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_REPRODUCED status=500`, after `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_ABSENT status=200`.
- Manual checks: forwarded `api.example.com:8443`→`8443`, `fastify.test`→`null`, plain `example.com:8080`→`8080`, IPv6 `[::1]:8443`→`8443`, non-proxy mode unchanged.
- `test/internals/request.test.js` (14 pass), `test/request-header-host.test.js` + internals (24 pass), `test/http-methods/get.test.js` (24 pass).

Remaining uncertainty:
- `test/trust-proxy.test.js` 6 subtests now fail plan-count because they assert `port == server.address().port` when `X-Forwarded-Host: fastify.test` (no port). Per docs/`host` semantics the correct value is now `null`. Those expectations encode the pre-fix bug; left untouched, not disabled.

